@startuml overview
' cumin-works - the states of an implementation issue in the implementation stage.
' A state is a label on GitHub, written without "cumin/status/". "do /" says who works in the state.
' A transition is written: action [guard] / what cumin does. A gray state belongs to another area.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.

hide empty description

state "ready" as Ready
Ready : do / cumin waits for a free slot

state "implementing" as Implementing
Implementing : do / the Implementer works

state "checking" as Checking
Checking : do / GitHub runs the required checks

state "awaiting-decision" as Decision
Decision : do / the Assignee answers

state "reviewing" as Reviewing #EEEEEE
Reviewing : (the review area)

state "awaiting-merge-decision" as MergeDecision #EEEEEE
MergeDecision : (the merge area)

[*] --> Ready : a Maintainer adds ready
Ready --> Implementing : request the implementation\n[cumin handles the ready, the blockers are closed,\ncumin has a free slot, no owner-task]\n/ cumin starts the Implementer
Implementing --> Checking : wait for the checks\n[no Implementer runs, the pull request passes]\n/ cumin links the pull request if needed
Implementing --> Implementing : request the implementation again\n[no Implementer runs, the pull request fails,\nno question, first time]\n/ cumin starts the Implementer again
Implementing --> Decision : stop the implementation\n[no Implementer runs, and: the Implementer asked,\nor the pull request fails after the retry,\nor the conflict resolution changed nothing]\n/ cumin notifies
Checking --> Implementing : request a check fix\n[a required check failed, below the limit]\n/ cumin starts the Implementer\nin the same session
Checking --> Decision : stop for failed checks\n[a required check failed, at the limit]\n/ cumin notifies
Checking --> Decision : stop for missing checks\n[a required check has no result\nafter the wait time]\n/ cumin notifies
Checking --> Implementing : request a conflict resolution\n[GitHub returns CONFLICTING]\n/ cumin starts the Implementer\nin the same session
MergeDecision --> Implementing : request a conflict resolution\n[GitHub returns CONFLICTING]
Checking --> Reviewing : [every required check passed]
Decision --> Ready : a Maintainer adds ready

@enduml
